{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 38, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "Fair traveler thou seekest a journey to Japan's hallowed land\nIn forty days thou shalt embark on a path most grand\nFrom thy departure point thou shalt take a flight to Tokyo's gate\nAnd upon arrival thou shalt find thyself in a city most great\n\nDay one thou shalt spend in Tokyo's streets so fine\nWandering through districts of Shibuya's busy design\nVisit the famous Shibuya Crossing where crowds doth throng\nAnd at night behold the neon lights of Harajuku's sweet song\n\nDay two thou shalt explore the temples of Senso-ji's might\nVisit the Asakusa district where ancient traditions take flight\nWalk the Nakamise Shopping Street where merchants doth sell\nThy treasures to take back to thine homeland to compel\n\nDay three thou shalt journey to Nikko where temples rise high\nVisit the Toshogu Shrine where the Tokugawa Shoguns lie\nMarvel at the beauty of the Kegon Falls so pure and bright\nAnd take a stroll through the gardens where cherry blossoms bloom in sight\n\nDay four thou shalt travel to Kyoto's city of peace\nVisit the Fushimi Inari Shrine where thousands of gates doth cease\nHike the trails of the Arashiyama Bamboo Grove so serene and still\nAnd behold the beauty of the Kinkaku-ji Temple's golden will\n\nDay five thou shalt explore the city of Osaka's savory delight\nVisit the Dotonbori district where street food doth shine so bright\nSample the local cuisine and drinks to tempt thy taste and whim\nAnd stroll along the river where boats doth glide with gentle brim\n\nDay six thou shalt journey to Hiroshima's city of peace and might\nVisit the Peace Memorial Park where history doth take flight\nWalk the Hiroshima Castle grounds where samurai once did stand\nAnd behold the beauty of the Miyajima Island's tranquil land\n\nDay seven thou shalt return to Tokyo's city of might\nVisit the Meiji Shrine where the spirits of the dead doth take flight